course: dictionary
lesson: 16068
title: Vouch for someone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To vouch for someone means to say that they are honest, good or telling the truth, and that you will take responsibility for it. «My aunt will vouch for me, so the club let me join.» The aunt puts her own good name behind the child.
explain: You can also vouch for something you have seen or tried yourself. «I can vouch for this pizza, because I ate two slices last night.» The speaker knows it is good from their own experience.
explain: Vouch almost always comes with for. Look at the words around it: if someone says «I know this is true» or «I'll stand up for you», they may be vouching. If someone says «I can't vouch for that», they do not know enough to say it is true.
fact: Vouch is a verb. Its forms are vouch, vouches, vouched and vouching.
fact: «Vouch for» means to say someone is honest or good, and to take responsibility for that.
fact: «Vouch for» can also mean to say something is good because you have seen or tried it yourself.
fact: «Can't vouch for» means you do not know enough to say that something is true.
exercise: «Mrs Patel said she would vouch for Sam when he asked for the library job.» What does vouch for mean here? | *Say he is honest and will take responsibility | Ask him to pay for the books | Tell him to go home | Hide him from the teacher
exercise: «I can vouch for this pizza, because I ate two slices last night.» Why can the speaker vouch for it? | *They have tried it themselves | Their friend said it was nice | They saw a picture of it | They read about it in a book
exercise: Mum will ____ for me at the school trip. Which word goes in the gap? | *vouch | fall | whisper | shout
test: «Can you vouch for the new boy?» What does vouch for mean? | Forget his name | *Say he is honest and good, and take responsibility | Ask him to leave | Give him a present
test: «I can't vouch for the film, I have not seen it.» Why can't the speaker vouch for it? | They are too busy to watch films | The film is too long | *They have not seen it, so they do not know it is good | They saw it twice and hated it
exam: «My teacher will vouch for my library card, so I can borrow books.» What does vouch for suggest? | The teacher is lending her books | The teacher is angry at the library | *Her teacher says the child is honest and will take responsibility | The teacher lost the card
